JobTitle, AccountEnabled |\n    Select-Object DisplayName, Department, JobTitle, AccountEnabled |\n    Export-Csv -Path \"C:\\Reports\\users.csv\" -NoTypeInformation\n```\n\n> **Key Concept:** Always include `-NoTypeInformation` with `Export-Csv`. Without it, PowerShell adds a `#TYPE` header row that clutters the output file.\n\n## SharePoint Site Usage Reports\n\nGather information about all sites or specific lists:\n\n```powershell\nGet-PnPList | Select-Object Title, ItemCount, LastItemModifiedDate |\n    Export-Csv -Path \"C:\\Reports\\lists.csv\" -NoTypeInformation\n```\n\n## Group Membership Reports\n\nExport the members of a specific group to a file:\n\n```powershell\n$group = Get-MgGroup -Filter \"displayName eq 'Engineering'\"\nGet-MgGroupMember -GroupId $group.Id -All |\n    ForEach-Object { Get-MgUser -UserId $_.Id } |\n    Select-Object DisplayName, UserPrincipalName, JobTitle |\n    Export-Csv -Path \"C:\\Reports\\engineering-members.csv\" -NoTypeInformation\n```\n\n## Formatting Output for the Console\n\nWhen reviewing data interactively (not exporting), use `Format-Table` and `Format-List`:\n\n```powershell\n# Table format — good for lists of items\nGet-MgUser -All | Format-Table DisplayName, Department, JobTitle -AutoSize\n\n# List format — good for detailed single-object views\nGet-MgUser -UserId \"pat@contoso.com\" | Format-List *\n```\n\n> **Key Concept:** `Format-Table` and `Format-List` are for **display only**. Never pipe formatted output to `Export-Csv` or other cmdlets — the data will be corrupted. Always use `Select-Object` before exporting.\n\n## Selecting Clean Output\n\nUse `Select-Object` to choose and rename columns for clean reports:\n\n```powershell\nGet-MgUser -All -Property DisplayName, CreatedDateTime |\n    Select-Object DisplayName,\n        @{Name=\"Created\"; Expression={$_.CreatedDateTime}} |\n    Sort-Object Created -Descending\n```\n\n## Scheduling Scripts\n\nTo run reports automatically, save your script as a `.ps1` file and use Windows Task Scheduler:\n\n1. Open Task Scheduler and create a new task.\n2. Set the trigger (e.g., daily at 7 AM).\n3. Set the action to run `pwsh.exe` (PowerShell 7) or `powershell.exe` with the argument `-File \"C:\\Scripts\\report.ps1\"`.\n\nFor scheduled scripts, use **app-only authentication** (certificate-based) so the script can run without a user signing in interactively.\n\n```powershell\n# Example: scheduled script header\nConnect-MgGraph -ClientId $appId -TenantId $tenantId `\n    -CertificateThumbprint $thumbprint\n# ... generate report ...\nDisconnect-MgGraph\n```\n0:{\"rsc\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-h-screen bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"sticky top-0 z-10 border-b border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/80 backdrop-blur-xl\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-3.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/sharepoint-m365\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-zinc-500 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-300\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M10.5 19.5L3 12m0 0l7.5-7.5M3 12h18\"}]}],\"SharePoint & M365 PowerShell\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/sharepoint-m365/bulk-operations\",\"className\":\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\",\"title\":\"Bulk Operations\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M15.75 19.5L8.25 12l7.5-7.5\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs tabular-nums text-zinc-500\",\"children\":[8,\" / \",8]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"h-8 w-8\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Automating Reports and Exports\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"lesson\":{\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Automating Reports and Exports\",\"description\":\"Generate reports and export data.\",\"slug\":\"automating-reports\",\"order\":8,\"prerequisites\":[\"m3-l7\"]},\"content\":\"$4\",\"exercises\":[{\"id\":\"m3-l8-ex1\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a pipeline that gets all users with their DisplayName and Department, selects those two properties, and exports the result to 'C:\\\\Reports\\\\users.csv' without type information.\",\"hints\":[\"Start with Get-MgUser -All -Property to request the fields.\",\"Pipe to Select-Object to pick DisplayName and Department.\",\"Pipe to Export-Csv with -NoTypeInformation.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-MgUser\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Start with Get-MgUser to retrieve users.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Select-Object\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pipe to Select-Object to choose properties.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Export-Csv\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pipe to Export-Csv to write the results to a file.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-NoTypeInformation\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Add -NoTypeInformation to prevent the #TYPE header row.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"C:\\\\\\\\Reports\\\\\\\\users\\\\.csv|C:/Reports/users\\\\.csv\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Export to 'C:\\\\Reports\\\\users.csv'.\"},{\"rule\":\"order\",\"sequence\":[\"Get-MgUser\",\"Select-Object\",\"Export-Csv\"],\"hintOnFail\":\"The pipeline order should be: Get-MgUser | Select-Object | Export-Csv.\"}],\"solution\":\"Get-MgUser -All -Property DisplayName, Department | Select-Object DisplayName, Department | Export-Csv -Path \\\"C:\\\\Reports\\\\users.csv\\\" -NoTypeInformation\",\"explanation\":\"This pipeline retrieves users, selects specific properties for a clean output, and exports to CSV. The -NoTypeInformation switch removes the metadata header row from the file.\"},{\"id\":\"m3-l8-ex2\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a pipeline that gets all lists from the current SharePoint site and displays them in a table with Title, ItemCount, and LastItemModifiedDate columns. Use -AutoSize for better formatting.\",\"hints\":[\"Use Get-PnPList to retrieve all lists.\",\"Pipe to Format-Table with the column names.\",\"Add -AutoSize for cleaner column widths.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-PnPList\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Get-PnPList to retrieve lists.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Format-Table\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pipe to Format-Table for tabular display.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Title\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Include the Title column.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"ItemCount\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Include the ItemCount column.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"LastItemModifiedDate\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Include the LastItemModifiedDate column.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-AutoSize\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Add -AutoSize for better column formatting.\"}],\"solution\":\"Get-PnPList | Format-Table Title, ItemCount, LastItemModifiedDate -AutoSize\",\"explanation\":\"Get-PnPList returns all lists on the site. Format-Table presents them in a readable table. -AutoSize adjusts column widths to fit the data. Remember: Format-Table is for display only, not for exporting.\"},{\"id\":\"m3-l8-ex3\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a pipeline that gets all users, sorts them by DisplayName in ascending order, and then formats the output as a list showing all properties.\",\"hints\":[\"Start with Get-MgUser -All.\",\"Pipe to Sort-Object with the DisplayName property.\",\"Pipe to Format-List with * to show all properties.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-MgUser\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Get-MgUser to retrieve users.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Sort-Object\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pipe to Sort-Object to sort the results.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"DisplayName\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Sort by the DisplayName property.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Format-List\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pipe to Format-List for detailed output.\"},{\"rule\":\"order\",\"sequence\":[\"Get-MgUser\",\"Sort-Object\",\"Format-List\"],\"hintOnFail\":\"The order should be: Get-MgUser | Sort-Object | Format-List.\"}],\"solution\":\"Get-MgUser -All | Sort-Object DisplayName | Format-List *\",\"explanation\":\"Sort-Object arranges the users alphabetically by DisplayName. Format-List * displays every property of each user in a vertical list format, which is useful for detailed inspection.\"},{\"id\":\"m3-l8-ex4\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a Select-Object expression that takes $users and creates output with a 'Name' column from DisplayName and a 'Email' column from UserPrincipalName, using calculated properties.\",\"hints\":[\"Pipe $users to Select-Object.\",\"Calculated properties use: @{Name=\\\"...\\\"; Expression={$_.PropertyName}}.\",\"Create two calculated properties: one for Name and one for Email.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"$$users\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Start with $users as the input.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Select-Object\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pipe to Select-Object.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"Name\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\\\"']Name[\\\"']\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Create a calculated property with Name='Name'.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"DisplayName\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Map the Name column from DisplayName using $_.DisplayName.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"Name\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\\\"']Email[\\\"']\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Create a calculated property with Name='Email'.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"UserPrincipalName\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Map the Email column from UserPrincipalName using $_.UserPrincipalName.\"}],\"solution\":\"$$users | Select-Object @{Name=\\\"Name\\\"; Expression={$_.DisplayName}}, @{Name=\\\"Email\\\"; Expression={$_.UserPrincipalName}}\",\"explanation\":\"Calculated properties in Select-Object let you rename columns and transform data. Each calculated property is a hashtable with Name (output column name) and Expression (script block that computes the value).\"},{\"id\":\"m3-l8-ex5\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write the command you would use as a Task Scheduler action argument to run a PowerShell 7 script located at 'C:\\\\Scripts\\\\report.ps1'. Just write the argument string that follows pwsh.exe.\",\"hints\":[\"Task Scheduler runs pwsh.exe with arguments.\",\"The -File parameter tells PowerShell to run a script.\",\"The argument is: -File \\\"C:\\\\Scripts\\\\report.ps1\\\"\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-File\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the -File parameter to specify the script path.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"C:\\\\\\\\Scripts\\\\\\\\report\\\\.ps1|C:/Scripts/report\\\\.ps1\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Specify the script path 'C:\\\\Scripts\\\\report.ps1'.\"}],\"solution\":\"-File \\\"C:\\\\Scripts\\\\report.ps1\\\"\",\"explanation\":\"When configuring Task Scheduler, you set the program to pwsh.exe and the arguments to -File followed by the script path. The -File parameter tells PowerShell to execute the specified script.\"}],\"moduleSlug\":\"sharepoint-m365\"}}],\"$L5\"]}],[\"$L6\"],\"$L7\"]}],\"isPartial\":false,\"staleTime\":300,\"varyParams\":null,\"buildId\":\"CCxR80sZRnjlIdOoXSFK7\"}\n5:[\"$\",\"footer\",null,{\"className\":\"border-t border-zinc-800/60\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/sharep